package webkit

// Prompt teaches agents to give a tool an interactive web frontend with the
// kit. It is short (tool descriptions are cut); kit/README.md, in the
// sandbox at /opt/aseman/webkit/README.md, has the whole guide.
const Prompt = `Interactive frontends: when people want to interact with a tool (operate it, forms, orders, filters, a dashboard they use, a console), build an interactive web page for it instead of relying on a generated frontend or ui_compose (those show results; a page does things). Write it in the sandbox (plain HTML is best), serve it, and expose it with proxy_create {port, start, title, tool}: it opens on the desk as the tool's card window, on the web, phones and desktops.
The page uses Aseman's web UI kit, so it looks exactly like the app and follows its theme: in <head> <link rel="stylesheet" href="/_aseman/kit/aseman-ui.css"><script src="/_aseman/kit/aseman-ui.js"></script>, <body class="t-page">. Every app component is a <t-…> element with the same props (kebab-case attributes, JSON values): t-column/t-row/t-grid (min-column-width)/t-card/t-section/t-tabs, t-text (variant h1-h5|body|caption), t-stat, t-chart (type line|area|bar|candlestick|pie|…; data, x, series|y), t-table (data, columns [{field, type, format}], search, selection), t-key-value, t-badge, t-quote, t-order-book, t-button (variant primary|tonal|…), t-text-field, t-dropdown, t-segmented-control, t-slider, t-switch, t-form, t-modal, t-callout, t-empty-state, t-skeleton…; gallery /_aseman/kit/gallery.html.
Calling the tool (the page's backend, as the person using it, through the Aseman API): declaratively call="Tool/microtool" args='{"city": {"path": "/form/city"}}' into="/fc" on buttons, forms (named fields become args) and <t-data call args into every> (loads, and reloads when bound args change; /fc__loading, /fc__error); in script await Aseman.call('Tool', 'microtool', args) (its value), Aseman.tools(), Aseman.show(tool, {microtool, args}). Data: Aseman.data (get/set paths); bind with bind-value="/form/city" or {"path": "/x"}; inputs write back; <t-show when>, <t-list each="/rows"><template>…</template></t-list>; client actions {"functionCall": {"call": "setValue|toggle|increment|showToast", …}}; formats number:2, compact, percent, currency:USD, date. Never hard-code colors or a theme (var(--t-primary), --t-series-1…).
Test it before telling anyone it is ready, and repeat until clean: proxy_get {probe: true}; open it in the desktop browser (aseman-desktop open …), screenshot it at ~360 px and ~1400 px wide, read the console for errors, and click every control, checking each call returns real data (no /x__error, no empty or MISSING values, nothing that does nothing). Check it is clean and standard (layout, formats, labels) and fits the tool and what was asked; fix what you find and test again.
Full guide: cat /opt/aseman/webkit/README.md (copy /opt/aseman/webkit/* to _aseman/kit/ in the served folder to check the page locally).`
